---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { buttonVariants } from '../../components/ui/Button';
---

<Layout title="Welcome to One Reader" description="A short guide to starting your first One Reader correspondence." indexable={false}>
  <header class="border-b border-border">
    <div class="shell flex min-h-20 items-center justify-between gap-6">
      <a class="font-serif text-[1.35rem] tracking-[-0.025em] no-underline" href="/" aria-label="One Reader, home">One Reader</a>
      <a class="text-sm text-muted-foreground underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground hover:underline" href="/member/">Your account</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main-content" class="shell py-16 sm:py-24">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-5">Welcome to One Reader</p>
      <h1 class="section-title max-w-2xl">A small note before you begin.</h1>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-9 text-muted-foreground">Thank you for joining One Reader. This is a service for writing to one person you do not know, without turning the exchange into a public performance. Here is how the room works.</p>

      <div class="mt-16 space-y-12 text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground sm:mt-20">
        <section aria-labelledby="start-heading">
          <h2 id="start-heading" class="font-serif text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.025em] text-foreground">Start with your account</h2>
          <p class="mt-4">Open your account and add the languages in which you are comfortable writing and reading. We also ask for your month and year of birth so younger and adult members remain in separate matching pools. You can choose whether you are available to receive letters; receiving and replying to conversations already open are available to every active account.</p>
          <a class={buttonVariants({ size: 'large' }) + ' mt-6'} href="/member/">Open your account</a>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="how-heading">
          <h2 id="how-heading" class="font-serif text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.025em] text-foreground">How a letter travels</h2>
          <p class="mt-4">You write an email to <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="mailto:write@onereader.co">write@onereader.co</a>. We remove the address you wrote from the letter, then look for one person who can read the language you chose and is available to receive a new correspondence. The matching system considers language, age group and recent activity, and avoids repeating recent pairs.</p>
          <p class="mt-6">The letter arrives from One Reader. The reader does not see your real email address. Each correspondence has its own private reply address: an opaque, randomly generated alias that belongs only to that conversation. Another conversation gets another alias. The underlying token is stored as a one-way hash rather than as a readable address.</p>
          <p class="mt-6">Replies keep using that same conversation-specific address. It remains active while the exchange is alive, and expires after 30 days without a reply. Either person can also click <em>End this correspondence</em> at the bottom of any conversation email. Ending one exchange does not affect another.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
          <h2 id="privacy-heading" class="font-serif text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.025em] text-foreground">What stays private</h2>
          <p class="mt-4">There is no public profile, follower count or feed. We use your email address to deliver the service, not to build an advertising audience or sell personal data. Letter contents are encrypted before they are stored, and real email addresses are kept away from the person on the other side.</p>
          <p class="mt-6">The annual membership is a small contribution to operating the service: €18 a year, just under five cents a day at the current price. It pays for delivery, storage, moderation and the work of keeping the room quiet. If two people decide they would rather continue outside One Reader, we are happy for the correspondence to become their own.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="advice-heading">
          <h2 id="advice-heading" class="font-serif text-2xl font-normal tracking-[-0.025em] text-foreground">A few things worth knowing</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
            <li><strong class="font-medium text-foreground">A reply is not a debt.</strong> Write when you have something to say, and allow the other person the same freedom. Silence is sometimes part of the exchange.</li>
            <li><strong class="font-medium text-foreground">Keep the room safe.</strong> Do not include passwords, financial details, exact addresses or anything you would not want a stranger to know. No sexual content, harassment, hate, spam or requests for personal information.</li>
            <li><strong class="font-medium text-foreground">Use the links in the email.</strong> You can end a correspondence or report a letter without replying to the other person.</li>
            <li><strong class="font-medium text-foreground">Membership is about new openings.</strong> One first letter is free. Annual membership lets you start one new correspondence every 24 hours, while receiving and replying remain available to active free accounts.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-5 border-t border-border pt-8">
        <a class={buttonVariants({ size: 'large' })} href="/member/">Set up my languages</a>
        <a class="text-sm text-muted-foreground underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground" href="/terms">Read the full terms</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <script>
    import { supabase } from '../../lib/supabase';

    const intentKey = 'dear-someone:signup-intent';
    const sessionResult = supabase ? await supabase.auth.getSession() : { data: { session: null } };
    const session = sessionResult.data.session;
    if (!session) {
      window.location.assign('/sign-in/');
    } else {
      const rawIntent = window.localStorage.getItem(intentKey);
      if (supabase) {
        try {
          const metadata = session.user.user_metadata ?? {};
          const intent = rawIntent
            ? JSON.parse(rawIntent)
            : metadata.plan_intent === 'free'
              ? {
                  source: 'signup',
                  plan: 'free',
                  countryCode: (navigator.language.split('-')[1] || '').toUpperCase() || null,
                  languageCode: navigator.language || 'en',
                  journalOptIn: metadata.journal_opt_in === true,
                  termsAccepted: metadata.terms_accepted === true,
                  privacyAcknowledged: metadata.privacy_acknowledged === true,
                }
              : null;
          if (intent) {
            const { error } = await supabase.functions.invoke('complete-signup', {
              body: intent,
              headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${session.access_token}` },
            });
            if (!error) window.localStorage.removeItem(intentKey);
          }
        } catch {
          // The account can still be completed from the account page.
        }
      }
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
